**Search and rejection summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across IMF, World Bank, SIS/cabinet releases, Reuters syndications, Carnegie, AFTE, Amnesty, HRW, CPJ, and Ahram. I kept 12 distinct URLs because they provided the clearest ruler-specific integrity nexus. I rejected or deprioritized country-level corruption indices and macro reports that did not connect to Sisi's personal conduct, duplicate syndications of the same Reuters/AP story, and later background material that only repeated the 2022 pattern without adding a new integrity claim. I also excluded welfare, poverty, and business-climate pages that were useful context but did not by themselves show personal dishonesty, self-dealing, or obstruction. Where official reform pledges appeared, I kept them only when paired with contrary evidence showing the gap between pledge and practice.

**Remaining gaps**
The biggest gap is direct evidence of personal or family enrichment: I did not locate a 2022 asset declaration, audit trail, procurement file, or court finding tying Sisi or his close family to specific private gain from office. A second gap is direct truthfulness/correction evidence from speeches or written retractions, so 7B.1 and part of 7B.2 remain inferential rather than forensic. The strongest evidence is instead on tolerated repression, selective clemency, and public reform pledges that were not matched by durable openness. More search would help if you want a sharper distinction between systemic patronage, military capture, and direct self-enrichment.

